{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D2","page":1,"quote":"11"},{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D33","page":1,"quote":"H7"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"IZBP"}],"comment":"The H7 hole (D33) on diameter D2 is a tight fit, but the part carries an IZBP plating callout in the title block with no allowance for coating thickness. Plating buildup will shrink the bore and can cause assembly interference; the designer should add a pre-plate tolerance or a note to ream/machine after plating."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Add a pre-plate undersize dimension for the H7 hole or specify that the hole is to be finished after IZBP plating."}]}
